WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.023
- It's Gabrielle Union!

00:00:03.573 --> 00:00:08.573
- Hi, hi, how is everyone?
How are you Drew?

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:09.650
- Oh Gabrielle,

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:12.230
I feel like I'm getting
to know you so well

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:13.817
through reading your book.

00:00:13.817 --> 00:00:16.550
- Oh, you're learning way too much.

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:17.970
(laughter)

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:20.360
- Oh, by the way, I was
watching all the press,

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:23.507
for "Bring It On: 20th Anniversary".

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:27.450
And is it true?
- It's true.

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:32.450
- Oh my God, I mean, I can't
even tell you, all day long,

00:00:33.587 --> 00:00:36.510
me and my girls sing the Toros song.

00:00:38.266 --> 00:00:41.130
I'm so excited.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:44.460
My daughters are going to freak out

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:45.810
that I was with you today.

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:48.158
And all night long we're
gonna be (clapping).

00:00:48.158 --> 00:00:50.921
♪ Brr it's cold in here ♪

00:00:50.921 --> 00:00:54.218
♪ There must be some
Toros in the atmosphere ♪

00:00:54.218 --> 00:00:57.900
♪ I said, o-ee-o-ee-o, ice, ice ice ♪

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.730
Oh my God it's so good!

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:01.578
Sorry I had to, sorry.

00:01:01.578 --> 00:01:02.411
(laughing)

00:01:02.411 --> 00:01:04.123
- It's okay, it's okay. You're not alone.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:08.747
- I'm sure you must
get that, all the time.

00:01:08.747 --> 00:01:09.580
- All the time.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:12.520
And I don't remember the cheer,
so that's like, thank you.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:17.520
- There's a video that went
viral of you and Kaavia.

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:22.690
She's upset about a bag,
and she started kicking it.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:27.480
Sometimes I literally think
my kids are the only one

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.330
who are behaving this way,

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:31.410
and it does make you feel like
you're alone on an island.

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:34.530
So there's not a Hallmark
greeting card for relief

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:37.350
and there should be 'cause
I think we all feel relieved

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.590
when we see other parents
going through the same thing.

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:40.432
- Yes!

00:01:40.432 --> 00:01:45.020
I started the motherhood
journey a little later

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:48.110
in the game, I'm a little
longer in the tooth

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:51.604
than I had imagined, when I was coming up.

00:01:51.604 --> 00:01:55.992
I assumed I would be a young mom,

00:01:55.992 --> 00:01:59.810
not a mom with lower
back pain and you know?

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:03.060
Who liked to listen to
Earth, Wind and Fire.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.420
So it's a little different but,

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:08.830
every day is like new surprise.

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:11.000
Like watching her with that backpack,

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:15.250
so all of us, my little
sister moved during Covid,

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:19.520
to help us with Kaav, and
we have this huge village,

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:21.620
but we're just watching
her and we're like,

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:23.010
where is she getting this from.

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:27.340
We're all relatively peaceful,
zen masters in this house,

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:29.830
so watching her, the rage.

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:31.440
Like we call it the ragey-rage,

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:32.850
like where did that even come from?

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:37.850
That just came from inside
of this little person.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:39.750
- Oh, I'm reading your book right now

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:42.830
and you had fire in
you when you were young

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:47.830
and like, I think you
are probably zen now,

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:50.840
because you took a whole
lifetime to get there.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:55.300
I love also your romantic,
beautiful love story with Dwayne.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:59.810
Listen relationship goals,
you know, we all need it.

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:02.450
How is it parenting with him?

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:05.050
- You know with each kid,
it's a little different.

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:08.220
Like, we definitely had to get
out of the one-size-fits-all

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:10.170
parenting rather quickly.

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:15.170
So I'm a stepmom to four kids
and we share Kaav together

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.480
and my husband started
his parenting journey

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:22.010
you know, pretty young,
and so I think over time

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:24.130
and then since we've been married,

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:27.910
we together have come into
a different parenting style.

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:32.670
So, with Kaav, we're very
much on the same page,

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:36.910
same with Zaya, but like
with the 18-year olds,

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:41.067
I am like this psychotic, overbearing,

00:03:41.067 --> 00:03:43.990
"What are you doing now?" kind of parent,

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:47.331
and my husband's like "Meh, whatever."

00:03:47.331 --> 00:03:49.407
They're gonna figure it out and I'm like,

00:03:49.407 --> 00:03:51.137
"But we can help them figure it out,

00:03:51.137 --> 00:03:53.543
"if we just hover over them!"

00:03:53.543 --> 00:03:56.610
So, I'm learning to kind of let go.

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:58.040
They're both away at school

00:03:58.040 --> 00:03:59.750
and it's really, really hard for me.

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:02.540
I probably talk to them
more now that they're gone

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:05.989
out of the house, than when we
were all under the same roof.

00:04:05.989 --> 00:04:10.989
It's terrifying, for me, having them be

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:14.850
across the country by
themselves on these new journeys

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:18.450
and we're not right there,
and it's driving me crazy.

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:20.453
And then the girl situation, I,

00:04:21.778 --> 00:04:25.380
I've become somebody
that I hated dealing with

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:28.090
when I was dating as a teen, I'm that mom.

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:30.530
- I look forward to my
daughter's date showing up

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:34.880
where I have like, a
sawed-off weapon, an NDA,

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:39.437
a chastity belt and a
taser, so I hear you.

00:04:39.437 --> 00:04:43.700
One thing, I have to mention
is I cannot stop eating these.

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:47.500
These are Bitsy's, your amazing new snack.

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:51.530
And by the way, very important,
they are school-safe,

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:52.870
which I really wanna press upon,

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:56.550
because that's such a
concern of a lot of parents.

00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:59.640
They are so delicious and amazing,

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:02.300
I've Googled, you can find
them at Amazon and Whole Foods

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:05.270
and any other vendors,
we'll put it on the website.

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:08.410
Parents, you're not gonna
believe how incredible these are.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:11.230
And we have more to talk
about with Gabrielle

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:13.840
that she is contributing and producing

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:16.210
and putting out into
the world, product wise.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:18.075
She is making the world

00:05:18.075 --> 00:05:20.676
a more delicious and beautiful place.

00:05:20.676 --> 00:05:23.259
(upbeat music)

